; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Mad Libs
; CATEGORY: Stories, Chatbots & Language
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     words, readword, sentences, story
; SUMMARY:  Asks you for a name, an animal, a food and other words, then drops them into a silly story.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Before you see the story, the program asks you for words: a name,
;   an animal, a describing word, a food and so on. It does not tell
;   you what the story is about, so the result is usually ridiculous.
;   The finished story is printed and also written on a paper scroll in
;   the turtle world.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and type one word for each question. If you just press
;   Enter, the program picks a word for you.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * READWORD to collect a word, MAKE to keep it in a variable
;   * SENTENCE to build a story from fixed text and your words
;   * a default value when the answer is empty
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Write a second story that uses the same words
;   * Ask for a plural noun and a verb ending in -ing
; ============================================================

; Ask for a word. If nothing is typed, use the backup word instead.
to collect :question :backup
  print :question
  localmake "w readword
  if or emptyp :w not wordp :w [print (sentence [I will use] :backup) output :backup]
  output :w
end

; The ~ at the end of a line joins it to the next one, so one long
; instruction can be spread over several lines.
to story
  output (list ~
    (sentence [One sunny morning,] :name [found a] :describing :animal [sitting in the kitchen.]) ~
    (sentence [The] :animal [was eating] :number [plates of] word :food ".) ~
    (sentence :name [shouted] word :shout "! [and the] :animal [ran off to] word :place ".) ~
    (sentence [Nobody has seen it since, but people say] :place [smells of] :food [to this day.]))
end

to scroll :lines
  clearscreen hideturtle
  penup setxy -360 -110 setheading 0 setpencolor 8 setpensize 2
  pendown filled [250 235 200] [repeat 2 [fd 240 rt 90 fd 720 rt 90]]
  ; rolled ends of the scroll
  penup setxy -360 130 pendown filled [220 200 160] [setheading 90 fd 720 rt 90 fd 16 rt 90 fd 720]
  penup setxy -360 -110 pendown filled [220 200 160] [setheading 90 fd 720 rt 90 fd 16 rt 90 fd 720]
  setpencolor 0 setlabelheight 16
  localmake "y 80
  foreach :lines [penup setxy -340 :y label ? make "y :y - 50]
end

make "name collect [Type a person's name:] "Grandma
make "animal collect [Type an animal:] "giraffe
make "describing collect [Type a describing word, like fluffy:] "enormous
make "number collect [Type a number:] 37
make "food collect [Type a food:] "spaghetti
make "shout collect [Type something you might shout:] "Yikes
make "place collect [Type a place:] "Paris
print []
make "lines story
foreach :lines [print ?]
scroll :lines
